body: |-
  Founder (2026-11-23): "i want gnomon to be this full 'jarvis' like suite that enables me to build seamlessly". On naming: "dimensions are the space where they are, and the mediums of which things are displayed are the named pieces like boards or doodles."

  What the team converged on (s1-scale-amendments.md):
  - Jinx's rule held: reserved fields nobody reads are untested contract. So no data bag, no pending state, no VR fields in S1.
  - What IS paid for now, because op rows are permanent: an open kind grammar with closed writes and a tolerant fold; first-class relations; refs on nodes; host-stamped provenance; project-scoped dimensions that outlive a session.
  - Three sign-offs became two (one modAbiId, one clientApiId move at S1.2).
  - First "talk and nodes appear" moment is S1.4, with no new code: a spoken turn is already session.send{source:'voice'}.

  Where the first draft was wrong (caught by Aegis, re-checked in code by the orchestrator):
  - "Host-stamped cause/hsid in the op payload" was not host-stamped: the mod builds the payload and the clamp passes it through (modhost/bridge.ts:76-83). Fix: the host overwrites a reserved payload key and sets row causes from the call in force.
  - refs[] on ref:v1 alone accepts any non-whitespace id, including card: and permit: schemes (ref.ts:85,128-144). Fix: a board allowlist.
  - tool.call carries no relayedFor at all today (mod-abi.ts:78; host.ts:845).
  - mod.command from the GUI is still refused pending a gesture proof (socket/dispatch.ts:912-914): a missed S1.3 dependency.

  Founder decisions the same night: live tray before images; T-DDL-01 clock starts at S1.4; if the usage bar is missed, stop the whiteboard medium but keep the dimension model and try the live tray.
